{"uid":"tools/guishot.py","name":"guishot.py","qualname":"tools/guishot.py","kind":"module","file":"tools/guishot.py","line":1,"end_line":112,"language":"py","signature":"","params":[],"returns":"","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"guishot -- a picture of the REAL Freedom window for the README.","description":"The window runs in a nested weston (Xvfb + weston, pixman renderer: the same display\nharness as guitime/guiscroll). The first URL is opened on the command line; every other\none in a new tab (xdotool: Ctrl+T, type, Enter), then the first tab is brought back to the\nfront, so the picture shows the tab strip, the omnibox and the connection badge of a real\nsession. FREEDOM_GUI_SHOT writes what the window's own painter drew (client-side\ndecorations included), so nothing of the virtual desktop leaks into the image.\n\nThe session is throwaway: HOME and FREEDOM_HOSTS_DIR point at a temporary copy of the\nrepository's config/, so the operator's profile, bookmarks and host lists are never read\nor written (the auto-allow of CDN hosts writes to allow.conf). A page pictured with its\nauthor CSS must be in the repository's allow.conf and js.conf (the trusted-host doctrine).\n\nUsage: guishot.py [--bin PATH] [--out PNG] [--wait S] URL [URL...]\nExit 0 when the picture was written, 1 when it was not, 2 when the environment is missing.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"","members":["tools/guishot.py::TAB_GAP_S","tools/guishot.py::KEY_DELAY_MS","tools/guishot.py::SHOT_PERIOD_S","tools/guishot.py::POINTER_PARK","tools/guishot.py::xdo","tools/guishot.py::main"],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
